# Which country tops the World Happiness Report?
subtitle: "Follow three clues to the country that tops the World Happiness Report, then find out what the survey really asks, and where money stops helping."
tags: ["psychology","economics","geography"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Guess the happiest\" stamp \"Not who you think\""

## Which country tops the World Happiness Report?
sources:
    - id: owid_hap
      title: Self-reported life satisfaction (Cantril ladder)
      authors: Our World in Data, from the World Happiness Report 2026 (Wellbeing Research Centre) and the Gallup World Poll
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/happiness-cantril-ladder
      finding: '2025 (average of 2023–2025): Finland 7.76, first, and first every year since 2017; Costa Rica 7.44, fourth; United States 6.82, 24th; Afghanistan 1.45, last'
    - id: owid_happy
      title: Happiness and Life Satisfaction
      authors: Esteban Ortiz-Ospina and Max Roser
      year: 2024
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/happiness-and-life-satisfaction
      finding: the Cantril ladder asks people to rate their current life from 0 (worst possible life for you) to 10 (best possible); richer countries tend to have higher average life satisfaction
    - id: owid_gdp
      title: GDP per capita
      authors: Our World in Data, from the World Bank
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/gdp-per-capita-worldbank
      finding: '2024, in 2021 international dollars: United States about $75,700, Finland about $55,900, Costa Rica about $27,300'

