    card title "Which is the world's happiest country?"

A: Which country tops the World Happiness Report? Let's play this one together. Here are four suspects.
    draw suspects

A: Clue one: it's rich, but about a quarter poorer per person than the United States. Clue two: its winters are long and dark.
    draw c1 c2

B: Denmark, then. Danes are always called the happiest people on Earth.
    highlight o_dk

A: Clue three: it has a long border with Russia.
    draw c3

    ask "Tap the country." choose ["o_us","o_dk","o_cr","o_fi"] answer o_fi
        right: Finland: about seven point eight out of ten, top for nine years running.
        wrong: Denmark used to win, but not lately.

    erase c1 c2 c3 suspects

B: Finland? Finns are famous for not smiling at strangers.
    draw ladder l0 l10

A: Which is the point: nobody is asked if they feel cheerful. They picture a ladder, from the worst possible life for them to the best, and say which step they stand on.
    draw g_fi

A: At the bottom is Afghanistan, at about one point four.
    group g_af members ["p_af","t_af","k_af"]

B: So money decides it. The United States must be right up there.
    highlight p_fi

A: Twenty-fourth, at about six point eight. Richer countries do tend to rate their lives higher, but not always.
    draw g_us

B: Then who beats America with less money?
    highlight p_us

A: Costa Rica: about a third of America's income per person, and fourth on the ladder. Money buys a few rungs, not the whole climb.
    draw g_cr

    highlight g_cr

